<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "rebalance">
<!ENTITY author    "FugginOld">
<!ENTITY repo      "Unraid-Rebalance">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.09.28">
<!ENTITY md5       "1e7dc552556c7af14963ae4dde132c03">
<!ENTITY launch    "Settings/ArrayRebalance">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&author;/&repo;/main/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY pkg       "&name;-&version;-x86_64-1">
<!ENTITY pkgURL    "https://github.com/&author;/&repo;/releases/download/&version;/&pkg;.txz">
<!ENTITY plugin    "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" launch="&launch;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        icon="balance-scale" min="6.12.0" support="https://github.com/&author;/&repo;/issues">

<CHANGES>
###2026.09.28###
**Added**
- The dashboard follows the Unraid display theme (Black, Gray, White or
  Azure) instead of always drawing a dark panel.
- The "Now moving" card shows the exact rsync command for the current move.
- After a dry run, a "View move script" pill jumps to a Move script panel
  that lists the planned moves as rsync commands, for review only. The
  script exits before its first command; Start rebalance rebuilds the plan
  and runs every safety check. A link next to "Download full log" opens it
  in a new tab.
- Keyboard focus rings and press feedback on buttons, links and inputs.

**Fixed**
- Empty folders are no longer planned or moved. Moving them freed no space,
  changed where new files land, and could hide the "Nothing can be moved"
  warning. (#7)
- "Nothing can be moved" now shows as a warning (amber status and message,
  and a warning notification) instead of a green Done. (#4)
- When the over-full disk has nothing in the included shares, the result
  now says so, instead of pointing at the free-space and size limits. (#4)
- A stop sent just as a paused run was resumed could be lost; it is now
  kept. (#6)
- At item depth 2 or 3, an item under a folder whose name contains a line
  break is skipped instead of breaking the plan.
- Settings inputs now have a border that stands out from the panel.

###2026.09.27###
**Fixed**
- A dry run that finds nothing to move now says why ("already balanced", or
  what kept an over-full disk from moving) and sends a notification, instead
  of showing "Dry run ready" with an empty plan.

###2026.09.26###
**Added**
- Pending "pause / stop after this move" requests are shown in the status pill,
  with a Cancel button.

**Fixed**
- Elapsed time and average rate no longer count time spent paused.
- A stop sent while paused could be lost; the control file is now written atomically.

###2026.09.25###
**Added**
- Initial release: proportional array rebalancing with a live web dashboard
  (Settings -> User Utilities -> Array Rebalance). Dry run, then disk-to-disk
  moves with pause / stop / abort, live progress and per-disk targets.
</CHANGES>

<!-- remove packages from older versions -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
rm -f $(ls &plugin;/&name;-*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v '&version;')
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- the package -->
<FILE Name="&plugin;/&pkg;.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>&pkgURL;</URL>
<MD5>&md5;</MD5>
</FILE>

<!-- post-install -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
chmod 755 &emhttp;/scripts/*
[ -f &plugin;/&name;.cfg ] || cp &emhttp;/default.cfg &plugin;/&name;.cfg
echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " Array Rebalance &version; installed"
echo " Settings > User Utilities > Array Rebalance"
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- uninstall -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
&emhttp;/scripts/rebalance-ctl abort >/dev/null 2>&amp;1
sleep 2
removepkg &pkg; >/dev/null 2>&amp;1
rm -rf &emhttp; /var/local/&name;
rm -f &plugin;/*.txz
echo "Array Rebalance removed (settings kept in &plugin;/&name;.cfg)"
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
